Below is a minimal example of a “rotating card” that spins around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform .6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;     /* Needed for 3D transforms */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Optional: add a back face so you can see something on the reverse side */
.card::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background: #f8f8f8;
  border-radius: 12px;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide when facing away */
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Place it behind the front face */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side content -->
    <h2 style="margin:0;padding:1rem;">Front Side</h2>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets the 3D perspective for the child element. |
| `.card` | The card itself; `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows children to keep their 3D position. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis when hovered. |
| `.card::after` | (Optional) Adds a back face that becomes visible after rotation. |

You can replace the `<h2>` with any content you like, or add more styling to the card’s front and back faces. Enjoy your rotating card!
